                <head>196. National Security Council Report<anchor n="1" xml:id="d196-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">NSC 5702</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1957-01-14"><hi rendition="#italic">January 14,
                        1957</hi>.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">NOTE BY THE EXECUTIVE SECRETARY TO THE NATIONAL SECURITY
                    COUNCIL ON EVALUATION OF ALTERNATIVE MILITARY PROGRAMS FOR KOREA</p>
                <list type="references">
                    <head>REFERENCES</head>
                    <item>A. NSC 5514<anchor n="2" xml:id="d196-f2"
                        /></item>
                    <item>B. NSC 5610<anchor n="3" xml:id="d196-f3"
                        /></item>
                    <item>C. Memo for NSC from Executive Secretary,
                        subject: “U.S. Objectives and Courses of Action in Korea”, dated October 12,
                            1956<anchor n="4" xml:id="d196-f4"/></item>
                    <item>D. NSC Actions Nos. 1486, 1560, 1607 and
                            1624<anchor n="5" xml:id="d196-f5"/></item>
                    <item>The enclosed draft report on the subject, prepared by the NSC Planning Board, is transmitted herewith for
                        consideration by the National Security Council at its meeting on Thursday,
                        January 24, 1957.</item>
                </list>
                <p>A Financial Appendix is also attached for the information of the Council.<anchor
                        n="6" xml:id="d196-f6"/></p>
                <p>The enclosure is intended as the first step in the review by the Planning Board
                    of the scope and allocation of military and non-military aid for Korea called
                    for by NSC Action No. 1624–c. In the light of
                    Council discussion of the enclosure as to the choice among the alternatives, the
                    Planning Board will subsequently prepare for Council consideration appropriate
                    revisions in NSC 5514, “U.S. Objectives and
                    Courses of Action in Korea”, in accordance with NSC Action No. 1624–c.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">James S. Lay,
                        Jr.</hi></signed><anchor n="7" xml:id="d196-f7"/></closer>



                <xi:include href="d196-a1.xml" xpointer="d196-a1"/>
